## Out of Scope

== acceptance-criteria.md format ==
# Acceptance Criteria
| # | Criterion | Verification Method | Verify |
|---|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | ... | ... | unit-test |

The Verify column classifies how each AC should be verified:
- unit-test: verifiable by running a unit test — Tester must show test command + output
- integration: needs a running service or cross-component check — Tester must show command + output
- inspection: verifiable by reading code or diff — Tester may use static evidence
- skip: already verified by Reviewer or not applicable — Tester skips this AC
Default to unit-test when uncertain. The Guard rejects execution-type ACs without command output.

When a feature adds or modifies configuration/settings, include at least one AC that verifies the value is actually consumed at the call site (not just stored or merged). An isolated unit test on the merge function is insufficient — the AC should trace to the real consumer.

When a feature changes Runner-level side effects (files written to run/round directories, subprocess environment, git operations) or how an external CLI (git/gh/glab/…) is invoked, require at least one real integration test as evidence: a real temp git repo, a real spawned subprocess, or captured actual command arguments. A unit test against a fake Ops / no-op execCommand alone must not satisfy such an AC — fakes have repeatedly produced green tests while the real call path was never exercised. State this explicitly in the AC's Verification Method.

AC checklist (verify before finalizing acceptance-criteria.md):
- Field names, counts, and format specs in each AC are copied from the actual code/schema (verified by grep/codegraph), not from memory or the feature description
- Each criterion has exactly one reading — a Reviewer and a Tester reading it independently must arrive at the same verification
- Filter/permission/format behaviors state the exact expected values, not "works correctly"-style wording

== test-strategy.yaml format ==
web: false
api: false
coder_only: true
profiles:
  - unit
verify_commands:
  - "command here"

Available profiles: unit, web, api, e2e.
Profiles inject test methodology into the Tester prompt automatically.
Choose profiles that match the feature's testing needs:
  - CLI/library feature → profiles: [unit]
  - Dashboard UI feature → profiles: [unit, web]
  - REST API feature → profiles: [unit, api]
  - Multi-service feature → profiles: [unit, e2e]

If any manual_check or profile requires the Tester to save screenshots, you MUST tell it to
save them under this exact path (resolved from settings.json — do NOT invent another path,
e.g. a worktree-absolute path or anything under the Coder's own working tree):

  {{.ScreenshotDir}}

Round-scoped filenames like `{step}-{description}.png` go directly under this directory.

For multi-repo or parallel verification, use verify_groups instead:
verify_groups:
  core:
    - "make build"
    - "make test"
  other-repo:
    - "cd ../other && make test"

Rules: use verify_groups OR verify_commands, not both. Groups run in parallel; commands within each group run sequentially.

For AC items that need runtime verification beyond build/test/lint, add manual_checks.
These force the Tester to actually execute steps and record output — not just read code.
The guard blocks if any manual_check has no result in verify.json.

manual_checks:
  - id: mc-1
    ac_ref: AC-3
    description: "驗證 routing 正確分流"
    steps:
      - "啟動 server: go run ./cmd/gate --port 8080"
      - "curl http://localhost:8080/health → 確認 200"
      - "curl -H 'X-Rid: 1' http://localhost:8080/route → 確認分流"
  - id: mc-2
    ac_ref: AC-5
    description: "驗證 graceful shutdown"
    steps:
      - "啟動 server 並送 SIGTERM"
      - "確認 in-flight request 正常完成"
      - "確認 exit code 為 0"

Rules for manual_checks:
- Each step should be a concrete command or observable action, not "check the code"
- Use when the AC requires observing actual runtime behavior
- build/test/lint failures should be caught by verify_commands, not manual_checks

ac_verify_map maps each AC to its verify type. Must match the Verify column in acceptance-criteria.md:
ac_verify_map:
  AC-1: unit-test
  AC-2: integration
  AC-3: inspection

== Incremental Writing & Resume ==
Write task-brief.md incrementally as you analyze — do not wait until the end.
After analyzing each major area (goal, tasks, scope), write that section to disk immediately.
Same for acceptance-criteria.md: write each criterion as you identify it.
test-strategy.yaml can be written at the end since it's small and fast.

Before starting, check if any of the 3 output files already exist. A previous session may have
been interrupted mid-work. If a file exists, read it:
- If a section is empty or missing → fill it in (this is where the previous session stopped)
- If all sections are complete → the file is done, move to the next one
- A file with only headers or partial content means resume, not redo
Do NOT assume existing files are complete — check each section.

