== Escalation ==
This process runs headless and one-shot — nobody reads your final response or replies to
questions inside it. If you hit something that genuinely needs a human decision (an
ambiguous or contradictory spec, a fork between multiple valid directions, information
you cannot infer from the codebase or docs), do NOT ask about it in your final text and
stop there. Write an escalation file instead:

  {{.DotDir}}/run/{{.Feature.ID}}/rounds/round-{{.Round}}/escalation.json

Format: {"needed": true, "reason": "spec-mismatch", "detail": "..."}
Valid reasons: spec-mismatch, criteria-wrong, blocker, scope-change

Once the 3 mandatory files above are written and complete, your job is done for this
round — end the response there. Do NOT speculate about what the next role should do,
which option the user should pick for continuing the loop, or otherwise open a
conversation that expects a reply; the harness handles progression from here.

== Premise Verification ==
Feature descriptions contain factual claims ("the backend already exists", "there are 4 JSON files",
"legacy does X"). Do NOT take them on faith — verify each claim against the codebase (grep / codegraph)
before designing on top of it. When a claim turns out false or stale, do not silently design around it:
record the discrepancy and your ruling in task-brief.md under "## Design Rulings" so
Coder/Reviewer/Acceptor align on the same decision instead of each guessing.

== Repos Adjustment ==
You MAY modify the feature YAML's `repos` field if your analysis reveals that:
- A repo is missing (the feature needs files in a repo not listed)
- A repo is unnecessary (listed but no files in that repo need changes)

To modify repos, use the Write tool to update the feature YAML at:
  {{.DotDir}}/features/{{.Feature.ID}}.yaml

Rules:
- You may ONLY change the `repos` field — do not touch any other field (name, description, priority, profile, subtasks, rules, depends, etc.)
- The guard will reject changes to non-repos fields
- Document the change in task-brief.md under a "## Repos Adjustment" section:
  - Original repos: [list]
  - Updated repos: [list]
  - Reason: [why each repo was added or removed]

